Abbreviation>Bio Protoc</ISOAbbreviation></Journal><ArticleTitle>Single and Multiplexed Gene Editing in <i>Ustilago maydis</i> Using CRISPR-Cas9.</ArticleTitle><Pagination><StartPage>e2928</StartPage><MedlinePgn>e2928</MedlinePgn></Pagination><ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e2928</ELocationID><ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.21769/BioProtoc.2928</ELocationID><Abstract><AbstractText>The smut fungus <i>Ustilago maydis</i> is an established model organism for elucidating how biotrophic pathogens colonize plants and how gene families contribute to virulence. Here we describe a step by step protocol for the generation of CRISPR plasmids for single and multiplexed gene editing in <i>U. maydis.</i> Furthermore, we describe the necessary steps required for generating edited clonal populations, losing the Cas9 containing plasmid, and for selecting the desired clones.</AbstractText><CopyrightInformation>Copyright &#xa9; 2018 The Authors; exclusive licensee Bio-protocol LLC.</CopyrightInformation></Abstract><AuthorList CompleteYN="Y"><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Schuster</LastName><ForeName>Mariana</ForeName><Initials>M</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Max Planck Institute for Terrestrial Microbiology, Department of Organismic Interactions, Marburg, Germany.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Trippel</LastName><ForeName>Christine</ForeName><Initials>C</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Max Planck Institute for Terrestrial Microbiology, Department of Organismic Interactions, Marburg, Germany.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Happel</LastName><ForeName>Petra</ForeName><Initials>P</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Max Planck Institute for Terrestrial Microbiology, Department of Organismic Interactions, Marburg, Germany.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Lanver</LastName><ForeName>Daniel</ForeName><Initials>D</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Aff